---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Describe only what the site actually does, and update this page before adding anything new.
const updated = '24 September 2026';
const contact = 'yw713@cam.ac.uk';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice | CUDGS">
    <article>
        <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
            This website is run by the Cambridge University Digital Gaming Society (CUDGS), a student society, which
            is responsible for any personal data described here. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
            Very little. There are no forms, advertising or cross-site tracking. The site only sets a cookie if you
            log in as a member (see below).
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Server logs:</strong> like almost every website, our server records each request's IP address,
                time and page, to keep the site running and secure. Logs are kept for 14 days, then deleted.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Visitor statistics:</strong> we count visits with Umami, which runs on our own server and
                uses no cookies. It records the page, the site you came from, your browser, device type and rough
                location (country or city), but not your IP address, and can't identify you. We use it only to see
                which pages are useful. We respect your browser's Do Not Track setting, and you can opt out below.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Events list:</strong> loaded from our public Google Calendar, with event pictures from Google
                Drive. Your browser connects to Google directly, so Google receives your IP address, under Google's
                privacy policy.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Instagram posts:</strong> if we show posts from our Instagram, they only load after you
                click to show them. Instagram (Meta) then receives your IP address and may set cookies, under
                Meta's privacy policy.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Links:</strong> Instagram, Discord and supporters' websites have their own privacy policies,
                which apply once you follow a link.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Member login</h2>
        <p>
            Members can log in with their University Account. Login is handled by Nevar, a service run by the Student-Run
            Computing Facility (SRCF): you enter your password on the University's own login page, never on our site.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>What we receive:</strong> your CRSid, and whether you're a current member of the University. We
                don't receive your name, email address or password.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>What we do with it:</strong> we look up your CRSid in the committee's membership list to show your
                membership type, expiry date and any member perks. The list holds each member's CRSid, name, membership
                type and expiry date, and is kept privately by the committee.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Login cookie:</strong> logging in sets one cookie, <code>cudgs_session</code>, which keeps you logged
                in for up to 7 days. It holds only your CRSid and an expiry time, is signed so it can't be altered, can't be
                read by scripts, and is deleted when you log out. It's strictly necessary for logging in, so it doesn't need
                your consent, and it isn't used for anything else.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Why:</strong> to run the society and give members access to their membership and perks, which is in
                the legitimate interests of the society and its members.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Mailing list</h2>
        <p>
            If you join the mailing list on the Members page, we store your name, your CRSid and, if you choose to give it,
            your college, in a private list kept by the committee. We use it only to email you about CUDGS events and news
            at your University address. You can leave at any time from the Members page (or by emailing us), which deletes
            your entry straight away. Each year's list is deleted at the end of that academic year.
        </p>

        <h2>Esports applications</h2>
        <p>
            If you apply for an esports team on the website, we store your CRSid and your answers (name, Discord username,
            game account, rank, roles, which leagues you're applying for, and your match-week and casual availability) in a
            private sheet. They're seen only by that game's reps and the President, and used only for team selection and
            scheduling. You can update your application at any time, or email us to have it deleted. Applications are deleted
            at the end of each season.
        </p>

        <h2>Opting out of statistics</h2>
        <p>
            <span class="optout-status">Your visits are counted.</span>
            <button type="button" class="optout">Don't count my visits</button>
        </p>
        <p class="note">This choice is saved in this browser only.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            Under UK data protection law you can ask what data we hold about you and have it corrected or deleted.
            Email us to do this. If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, you can complain to the
            Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>
    </article>
</Base>

<script>
    // Umami skips tracking when localStorage has umami.disabled = 1.
    const KEY = 'umami.disabled';
    const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.optout-status')!;
    const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.optout')!;

    function render() {
        let off = false;
        try {
            off = localStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1';
        } catch {}
        status.textContent = off ? "Your visits aren't counted." : 'Your visits are counted.';
        button.textContent = off ? 'Count my visits again' : "Don't count my visits";
    }

    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        try {
            if (localStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1') localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
            else localStorage.setItem(KEY, '1');
        } catch {}
        render();
    });
    render();
</script>

<style>
    .optout {
        margin-left: 0.75rem;
        padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--cam-blue);
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        font: inherit;
        color: var(--cam-blue);
        background: none;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    .optout:hover,
    .optout:focus-visible {
        color: var(--black);
        background: var(--cam-blue);
    }

    .note {
        font-size: 0.6rem;
        color: #B5BDC8;
    }

    article {
        padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 2;
        background: rgb(14 17 22 / 0.9);
    }

    h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 0.9rem + 1.5vw, 2rem);
        color: var(--cam-blue);
        text-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--cam-dark-blue);
    }

    h2 {
        margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--cam-blue);
    }

    .updated {
        color: #B5BDC8;
    }

    p,
    ul {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    li + li {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }

    a {
        color: var(--cam-blue);
    }
</style>
